<http://data.silknow.org/event/ea0d5662-d32c-3559-a575-db89d8e3f8c3>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "John Jones Bequest. Acquired as Spanish, 17th century.\n\nConservation in 2017 involved the reattaching of numerous loose veneers and the removal of a discoloured and brittle shellac varnish.\n\nAttribution\nIt is now considered probable that the frame was made in Jerusalem during the 19th century where there was a signficant production of mother of pearl devotional souvenir items by Franciscan communities."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/5cf152cb-950e-32d8-b6cf-d60c570193c2> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Bequeathed by John Jones" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6d84b73f-b4bd-32fe-b255-bd49453cef20> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "John Jones Bequest. Acquired as Spanish, 17th century.\n\nConservation in 2017 involved the reattaching of numerous loose veneers and the removal of a discoloured and brittle shellac varnish.\n\nAttribution\nIt is now considered probable that the frame was made in Jerusalem during the 19th century where there was a signficant production of mother of pearl devotional souvenir items by Franciscan communities."@en .

